reference.api:
```
GET  /v1/availability?role=&from=&to=&tz=        → open slots (interviewers x time)
POST /v1/interviews {candidate, loop, slot_id, idempotency_key} → 201 {interview_id}
POST /v1/interviews/{id}/reschedule | /cancel
POST /v1/sessions/{id}/join                       → {token, ws_url, rtc_token}
WS   /v1/sessions/{id}/edit                       (ops in, ops out, cursor, presence)
POST /v1/sessions/{id}/run {language, code}       → 202 {run_id}; result over WS
PUT  /v1/interviews/{id}/feedback {scores, decision, notes}
```
- Join tokens are short-lived, signed, bound to one session and role (candidate, interviewer, observer).
